// names the gate looks up by text, never by a resolved token (G.regionCapText, G.isAtomOp, G.isMutOp, G.f2In "Ptr", G.testCapText)
// shortcut: kept by hand; a new Nm.lit lookup of a unit name in G must be added here, else a closure check misses that unit
// prompt: the unit names the gate looks up by text: Srs.Region, ACell, Cell, Ptr, Test, and the capabilities of the write and atomic builtins (Gate.mutCap, Gate.atomCap; missing them made NegTest closures accept s2 negs array_put_nomut, cell_nomut, atom_noeffect); every closure check (NegTest children, --emit) adds them as roots
def Kernel.implicitRoots(): Os.Strs = Os.More("Srs.Region", Os.More("ACell", Os.More("Cell", Os.More("Ptr", Os.More("Test", Os.More(Gate.mutCap(), Os.More(Gate.atomCap(), Os.End)))))))

